#!/usr/bin/env bash
# scripts/campfire-archive-files — write the campfire archive's README and
# Playwright config into an emitted tree.
#
# Split out of scripts/build-campfire-archive so the two documents that
# define the archive's CONTRACT are readable as documents rather than as
# heredocs buried in a pipeline. The README is executable: scripts/smoke
# extracts its fenced ```sh blocks and runs them, skipping `## Run` and
# `## Regenerate`. Change a command here and you change what CI runs.
#
# Usage: campfire-archive-files TREE ROUNDHOUSE_SHA CAMPFIRE_SHA SPINEL_VERSION

set -euo pipefail

TREE="${1:?tree}"
ROUNDHOUSE_SHA="${2:?roundhouse sha}"
CAMPFIRE_SHA="${3:?campfire sha}"
SPINEL_VERSION="${4:?spinel version}"

cat > "$TREE/README.md" <<README
# ONCE Campfire → spinel

[ONCE Campfire](https://github.com/basecamp/once-campfire) — Basecamp's
MIT-licensed chat app — transpiled from its Rails source by
[Roundhouse](https://rubys.github.io/roundhouse/) and compiled
ahead-of-time to a native binary by the
[Spinel](https://github.com/matz/spinel) Ruby VM.

This is **source**, not a binary: you compile it for your own platform.
Building takes a few minutes — it is one whole-program C compile.

Running it serves campfire on http://localhost:3000 (set \`PORT\` to
override), with live updates over the \`/cable\` WebSocket. The first
visit lands on campfire's own first-run page, which creates the account,
the first user, and the first room; the database is created on demand at
\`storage/development.sqlite3\`.

## Provenance

| | |
|---|---|
| roundhouse | \`$ROUNDHOUSE_SHA\` |
| once-campfire | \`$CAMPFIRE_SHA\` |
| spinel (at build time) | \`$SPINEL_VERSION\` |

Spinel tracks its master branch unpinned, so a much later checkout may
behave differently from the one this archive was generated against.

## Prerequisites

- [spinel](https://github.com/matz/spinel) — \`spinel\` and \`spin\` on PATH
  (the repo's \`bin/\` after \`make\`)
- A C toolchain + SQLite headers (\`libsqlite3-dev\`) — the binary links \`-lsqlite3\`
- Node.js 18+ — for the End-to-end suite

## Build

\`\`\`sh
spin build
\`\`\`

## Run

\`\`\`sh
./build/bin/campfire
\`\`\`

## End-to-end

Browser tests (Playwright) driving the built binary. The config boots the
server itself, so run this after Build. Static assets ship prebuilt in
\`static/assets/\`, so no Ruby and no asset pipeline are needed:

\`\`\`sh
cd e2e
npm install
npx playwright install chromium
npx playwright test
\`\`\`

These mirror \`scripts/campfire-cable-drive.rb\` — the cable walk — in a
real browser: two tabs sign in, both open room 1, one posts a message and
both receive it live; and a lifted stream name is refused by the stock
Turbo channel. Each spec names which of the walk's checks it stands for.

## What is not in this archive

- **Attachments and avatar variants** — no blob storage, no image
  processor. The attachment test fixtures are stripped (they were 50 MB).
  User avatars currently answer 500 (a \`to_param\` gap in the
  transpiler's runtime, ledgered), so pages show broken avatar images.
- **Web push.** Every message you post will print

  \`\`\`
  [job] a queued job raised: uninitialized constant ThreadPoolExecutor
  \`\`\`

  on stderr: campfire enqueues a web-push delivery job per message, and
  the job dies at its thread-pool constructor because the delivery
  machinery (a keep-alive HTTP client and a \`Concurrent\` thread pool)
  is not modeled. The job is dropped; the message itself is unaffected —
  it was already broadcast to the room before the job ran. Expected
  output, not a crash.
- **The native test binaries.** The emitted \`test/\` sources ship, but
  \`spin test\` is not wired into this README: several test programs do not
  compile or do not pass today, and a \`## Test\` section that is red is a
  section nobody reads. The browser suite above is what this archive
  asserts. This is the next thing to land, not a permanent gap.

## Regenerate

\`\`\`sh
roundhouse --target spinel -o <output-dir> <path-to-once-campfire>
\`\`\`
README

cat > "$TREE/e2e/playwright.config.js" <<'CONFIG'
import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test'

// Generated by Roundhouse for the published campfire archive.
//
// UNLIKE the in-repo config this is derived from, it carries a
// `webServer` block. In the repo, `scripts/campfire-e2e` owns the server
// lifecycle and the config deliberately has none; in the archive there is
// no such script, and `scripts/smoke` runs the README's steps verbatim —
// so the suite has to boot the binary itself.
//
// NO SEED STEP, and no sqlite3 CLI. The binary creates its own database
// on first boot and campfire's own first-run page creates the account,
// the first user and room 1; `signIn` in helpers.js takes that branch
// when it lands there. That is what makes this archive runnable with
// nothing but spinel, a C compiler and Node.
//
// NOT PARALLEL, one worker: every spec drives ONE campfire over one
// SQLite file opened `default_transaction_mode: immediate` — a single
// writer — and every spec is in the same room.
export default defineConfig({
  testDir: '.',
  fullyParallel: false,
  // EVERY SPEC IS A "SECOND CLIENT", so every spec pays the stall.
  // Playwright gives each test its own browser context, and a
  // single-worker Tep server parks inside the first connection's
  // keep-alive loop instead of returning to accept() — measured at ~30s
  // before a new client is served (docs/pipeline/runtime.md § A
  // single-worker Tep server serializes on one keep-alive connection).
  // Playwright's 30s default expires INSIDE that window, so at the
  // default only the first spec in a run can pass.
  //
  // 90s is a workaround for a ledgered defect, not a considered budget.
  // Drop it back to the default when that entry closes.
  timeout: 90_000,
  workers: 1,
  forbidOnly: !!process.env.CI,
  // No retries: a retry turns a flaky asset 404 into a green run, and
  // catching exactly that is why the asset spec exists.
  retries: 0,
  reporter: process.env.CI ? [['github'], ['list']] : 'list',
  use: {
    baseURL: 'http://localhost:3000',
    trace: 'on-first-retry',
    // campfire's own system tests run 1400x1400; below that breakpoint
    // the room layout moves the sidebar and hides the composer.
    viewport: { width: 1400, height: 1400 },
  },
  webServer: {
    command: './build/bin/campfire',
    cwd: '..',
    url: 'http://localhost:3000/',
    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,
    timeout: 120_000,
  },
  projects: [
    { name: 'chromium', use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] } },
  ],
})
CONFIG
